desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Python36 Compatibility Ssl"
	title_zh: "Python36 Compatibility Ssl"
	type: compatibility
	level: high
	rule_id: "source-compatibility-python36-compatibility-ssl"
	risk: "Compatibility"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `python36-compatibility-ssl` (python/lang/compatibility/python36.yaml).
Original message: this function is only available on Python 3.6+
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal Semgrep pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review this occurrence and replace it with a safer alternative.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.py": <<<POS
ssl.get_ciphers()
POS
	"safefile://pos.py": <<<NEG
ssl.get_protocol_name()
NEG
)

${*.py}.pattern_regex(/(?:ssl\.get_ciphers\(\))/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "high",
	title: "Python36 Compatibility Ssl",
	title_zh: "Python36 Compatibility Ssl",
	message: "Python36 Compatibility Ssl detected.",
}
